; VBoxContainer's vertical solve, drawn as flat bands.
;
; The one variable: where each row's top edge lands. Two columns hold the SAME
; four children with the SAME `custom_minimum_size` heights (60, 40, 40, 90) and
; the SAME `theme_override_constants/separation = 24`, so the only thing that
; can move a band is the solve itself — there is no text, no stylebox and no
; texture in this scene to blame a wrong edge on.
;
; Left column pins the EXPAND path. Its four minimums plus three separations
; come to 302 of the container's 542, and the two middle rows carry
; `size_flags_vertical = 3` at stretch ratios 1 and 2. `_resort` does NOT split
; the 240 leftover and add it to each minimum — it recomputes each stretcher's
; WHOLE size as `stretch_avail * ratio / total` over a `stretch_avail` that
; already carries their minimums (80 + 240 = 320), then truncates. Godot 4.6.3,
; band edges read off its own render at x=300: Red 60..119, Blue 144..249 (106),
; Green 274..486 (213), Amber 511..600 (90), with one pixel of the 320 left
; unassigned at the bottom. Reconstructing it as "minimum plus a share of the
; leftover" gives 120 and 200 instead, which is 14 px of drift by the third band.
;
; Right column pins the PITCH with nothing stretching: identical minimums, no
; expand flags, `alignment = 1`. The stack keeps its natural 302 and Godot
; centres it, so the first band starts 120 px down (Red 180..239, Blue 264..303,
; Green 328..367, Amber 392..481). That case is the one a broken running-offset
; shows up in most plainly, and it is dead in the left column — `alignment` only
; applies when nothing stretched.
;
; The truncation carries a fractional-error accumulator, and the engine runs it
; in float32 while we run it in float64: at 320/3 the two fractions sum to just
; under 1 in float and just over it in double, so our Green is 214 rather than
; 213 and Amber follows one pixel down. The baseline below is OURS and carries
; that pixel; every other edge in the frame matches Godot exactly.
;
; Every other golden in the set draws its 2D content at authored coordinates.
; None solves a container at all, so a row pitch that dropped `separation`, or
; shared leftover space by count instead of by stretch ratio, would move no
; baseline anywhere else.

